decisions:
  - id: d-flow-merge-precedence
    decision: flow_check merges flows.yaml + flow-index.json with flows.yaml winning on id collision
    rationale: Preserves existing explicit flows.yaml validation behavior while extending coverage to .purpose-defined flows; least-surprising precedence.
  - id: d-version-6.6.2
    decision: Bump paradigm + paradigm-mcp + plugin to 6.6.2 (patch)
    rationale: Bugfix-only release with MCP tool behavior changes (pm_postflight, flow_check, purpose_add_flow); paradigm-mcp bumps because tool behavior changed.
learnings:
  - 'When two Paradigm validators disagree about the same artifact, suspect duplicated resolution logic — the canonical fix is to route both through the same shared helper (here: resolveAnchorPath) rather than patch each call site.'
  - pm_postflight had reimplemented aspect-anchor path resolution inline instead of using the shared resolver aspect_check uses — a latent divergence that made aspect-anchors unsafe to set to block repo-wide.
  - flow_check read only flows.yaml while purpose_add_flow/reindex use .purpose-derived flow-index.json — two unsynced flow registries; fix merges both with flows.yaml winning on id collision.
  - The real failure case for the flow_check bug is when flows.yaml is absent entirely, so the merge must happen before the empty-check early-return, not just inside the inner lookup branch (caught by reviewer).
